# Uperf-Linux per-application power mode mapping
# Format: <process_pattern> <mode>   (space or colon separated)
# Patterns are matched case-insensitively as substrings of /proc/[pid]/comm and
# /proc/[pid]/cmdline.
# Modes: balance, powersave, performance, fast
#
# ORDER MATTERS: the first matching rule wins, so a specific pattern has to be
# listed before a broader one that also occurs inside it. "steam_app_730"
# contains "steam", so any rule keyed on "steam" placed first would capture
# every Steam game and hold it at balance.

# --- Steam titles and the layers that run them -----------------------------
# These come first because they are the most specific: a Steam game is executed
# as steam_app_<appid>, and on this architecture it runs under box64, FEX or
# Proton. All of them are the heaviest workloads the device will see.
steam_app_                      performance
box64                           performance
box86                           performance
FEXBash                         performance
FEXInterpreter                  performance
FEXCore                         performance
gamescope                       performance
proton                          performance
wineserver                      performance
wine                            performance

